The verify_dfa function contains the vulnerable differential encoding verification logic. Specifically, lines 228-238 show the loop that uses a single mark (MARK_DIFF_ENCODE) and incorrectly assumes that any backward transition (k < j) indicates a transition to an already-verified state:

c
		for (j = i;
		     (BASE_TABLE(dfa)[j] & MATCH_FLAG_DIFF_ENCODE) &&
		     !(BASE_TABLE(dfa)[j] & MARK_DIFF_ENCODE);
		     j = k) {
			k = DEFAULT_TABLE(dfa)[j];
			if (j == k)
				goto out;
			if (k < j)
				break;		/* already verified */
			BASE_TABLE(dfa)[j] |= MARK_DIFF_ENCODE;
		}

This allows loops in the differential encoding chain to bypass verification, which is the exact root cause of the vulnerability.
